"""Authorial questions merged by mathematical content after source reading."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];P=[]
T1='MPL_137_002-044_transcription.tex';T2='MPL_137_045-086_transcription.tex'
def add(n,title,occ,source,today,art,why,worth,refs):
    P.append(dict(id=f'MP-SA09-{n:02}',title=title,occurrences=occ,as_he_states=source,plausible_today=today,state_of_art=art,why_open=why,worth=worth,refs=refs))
    W.joinpath('problems.json').write_text(json.dumps(P,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
add(1,'Weightwise PD de Rham comparison',[T1+':113-130 (137/4)',T2+':998-1002 (137/73-74)'],'Construct the displayed weight-n comparison, with its terminal map an isomorphism onto the kernel; later obtain the evaluated complex through degree n. CL-SA09-137-004; SA09-27/28/29.','For a specified exact category of finite models and an admissible left-exact F, prove a natural homotopy equivalence with good τ≤nF(C•), then separately test products and PD structure. Do not assert unbounded integral reconstruction.','Dold–Puppe1961 §§2-4 and SGA4 XVII5.5 give the homotopical tools; Sullivan1977 Theorem10.1 is rational. No opened source gives the exact full structured comparison.','The local theorem gives no complete comparison construction; the later paragraph retracts the untruncated wording. The source does not explain a historical abandonment.','High value: an explicit low-weight comparison can determine whether the source’s exact kernel and truncation conventions support the proposed construction.',['DoldPuppe1961','SGA4XVII','Sullivan1977'])
add(2,'Nonlinear preservation of special complexes',[T1+':316-318;368-430 (137/10-12)'],'The tensor-closure proposition is extended tentatively to Λ,Γ,Sym and marked false. CL-SA09-137-008.','Retain reduced nonlinear operations on contractible simplicial projective generators; do not expect projective homology after powers of arbitrary sphere objects.','Dold–Puppe1961 develops non-additive derived functors; our exact Γ²K(Z,1) computation gives H₁=Z/2. The problem is resolved negatively for the broad closure claim.','The manuscript supplies its own false marks; no further historical reason is needed.','Low value as a new theorem: preserve the counterexample and use it to choose the correct domain for later operations.',['DoldPuppe1961','SGA4XVII'])
add(3,'Which Hilbert polynomials are realizable?',[T1+':436-460 (137/13)'],'For prescribed homology ranks ν_j, at what conditions does a strictly special object with rank polynomial f exist? CL-SA09-137-010.','For finite-support ν_j, the shifted Newton expansion of f−Σν_jbinom(t,j) must have μ₀=0 and all μ_i≥0; construct the finite direct sum of disks and spheres.','The source answers this question; proof_audit.md §1 and outputs/recompute.json check the formula and Euler value. Dold–Puppe §3 gives the rank conversion.','It did not stay open on the page; the displayed answer needs finite support and the integer-valued polynomial convention.','Low research priority: useful as a normalization test for the companion edition.',['DoldPuppe1961','StacksDK'])
add(4,'Extend PID dévissage to Dedekind or general bases',[T1+':573-579 (137/16)',T1+':1519-1523 (137/38)'],'Dedekind à la rigueur; later consider more general coefficient rings. CL-SA09-137-015/019/023.','For a Dedekind domain, replace free coefficients by finite projectives and retain ideal-class and torsion-module data; specify commutativity for symmetric tensor and divided powers. General rings require an exact/projective-complex formulation rather than elementary scalar disks.','The opened PID theorem is Rasmussen–Marchand2019 §3.3; SGA6 I4.8 gives finite-projective complexes over general rings. The invertible ideal counterexample in proof_audit.md §1 proves rank alone cannot be the extension.','No complete general-base classification is supplied; the source only suggests it. No biographical reason for dropping it was found.','Moderate value: one run can formulate the Dedekind replacement precisely and identify which later universal constructions survive.',['RasmussenMarchand2019','SGA6I'])
add(5,'Complete the intrinsic additive brick category',[T1+':896-1209 (137/23-28)'],'Axiomatize spheres, disks, extension classes and finite sums; composition is omitted as evident. CL-SA09-137-018/019.','Specify a preadditive category including scalar composition tables, boundary S₀, nonzerodivisor assumptions and an explicit ambient exact structure for Ext¹. Compare its finite additive envelope with bounded PID complexes.','The chain-map equations and matrix compositions are checked in proof_audit.md §3. Isbell1960 explains generation by adequate subcategories; Bühler Definition2.1 gives the missing exact-structure vocabulary.','The source acknowledges omitted composition and leaves the category scope inconsistent between C and C₀.','Moderate value: a finite presentation with boundary cases is a tractable editorial and verification task, not a broad new classification.',['Isbell1960','Buhler2009','RasmussenMarchand2019'])
add(6,'Recover tensor and Γ operations on coefficient functors',[T1+':1193-1209 (137/28)',T1+':1529-1547 (137/38)',T2+':850-972 (137/67-71)'],'La chose restante à faire and Notre propos principal ask to express F(M)⊗F(N)→F(M⊗N) and Γ^iF(M)→F(Γ^iM) as extra cochain structure. CL-SA09-137-023/039/040.','Define the strict operations and all units, substitutions and naturality maps on a precise admissible functor category; prove extension from generators before comparing to an operadic model.','Dold–Puppe§2 and Richter2009 §§6-7 describe transported tensor on chains; Richter Remark7.7 leaves a direct higher-PD characterization open there. Berger–Fresse2004 constructs coherent cochain operations in a different concrete model.','The text moves from linear dévissage to this task explicitly; its factorization question and missing unit show unfinished construction.','Very high value: resolving the local extension and coherence data is the necessary first step toward every reconstruction comparison.',['DoldPuppe1961','Richter2009','BergerFresse2004'])
add(7,'Density, dual density and restriction of functors',[T1+':1213-1398 (137/29-34)'],'The canonical presentation and restricted nerve are identified with generation by colimits; restriction of colimit-preserving functors is marked à vérifier, with an equivalence clause deleted. CL-SA09-137-020/021/022.','Use canonical density and codensity, or the finite additive-enriched envelope. Restriction is fully faithful when the indicated canonical presentations are preserved, and the finite additive case is a matrix equivalence.','Isbell1960 introduction and §1.3-1.5 supply the adequate-subcategory and conjugacy framework. Our scalar-homogeneous nonadditive map disproves the weaker Set-valued finite-sum shortcut.','The handwritten verification is omitted and one overstrong claim is false; the standard correction was already available.','Moderate editorial value: identify the intended enriched statement and limits, but do not market it as a new higher-density theorem.',['Isbell1960'])
add(8,'Compare structured cochains with de Rham data in both directions',[T1+':1545-1567 (137/38-39)',T2+':998-1002 (137/73-74)'],'Il faudrait examiner whether de Rham–Sullivan or PD de Rham determines the supplementary structure; the reverse direction is called clear. CL-SA09-137-024/042.','Over Q-algebras, compare fully specified structured cochains with an appropriate rational CDGA model; integrally specify a PD/enriched category and weak equivalences, and prove separate functors and inverse comparisons.','Sullivan1977 Theorem10.1 supplies the rational homotopy benchmark. Horel Theorem5.4, Mandell MainTheorem and Toën Theorem0.1 use distinct integral enhancements and do not identify this precise datum.','Neither direction is constructed on the leaf; characteristic0 is too short a hypothesis for factorial arguments. No source explains why the author stopped here.','Very high interest but limited one-run reach: begin with one exact functor and low-degree operation compatibility.',['Sullivan1977','Horel2024','Mandell2006','Toen2020'])
add(9,'How much homotopy type do the supplementary operations recover?',[T1+':1551-1567 (137/39)',T2+':977-1002;1304-1310 (137/72-74,86)'],'Il faut voir dans quelle mesure the structure reconstructs the homotopy type. No connectivity or finiteness class is specified. CL-SA09-137-024.','Distinguish conservativity, recognition of objects, recovery of mapping spaces and inverse realization; test a specified model on connected nilpotent finite-type spaces before widening scope.','Sullivan1977 Theorem10.1 is rational; Mandell2006 is faithful and recognizes integral finite-type nilpotent objects but not full; Horel2024 Theorems5.4/6.1 gives binomial recovery/integral completion; Toën2020 Theorem0.1 is simply connected finite type.','PursuingStacks§119 reports failure of a particular later divided-power-derived comparison and proposes a binomial alternative; it is not a blanket retraction of this question.','High long-term interest: a few hours can isolate the correct source category and test K(Z,1), K(Z,2) and torsion examples, not prove the whole programme.',['Sullivan1977','Mandell2006','Horel2024','Toen2020','GrothendieckPS1983'])
add(10,'Freeness versus Karoubi completion',[T1+':1727-1763;1789-1827 (137/41-42)',T2+':51-141 (137/46-47)'],'A cancelled Karoubian claim is followed by admitting that every finite-free summand is free; later an idempotent-complete target is required. CL-SA09-137-026/029.','Use finite projective coefficients and the Karoubi envelope over general commutative rings; retain finite-free models only under the explicit freeness assumption.','SGA6 I4.8 treats finite projectives; Bühler§6 gives idempotent completion; Dold–Puppe normalization uses split idempotents in additive targets.','The text itself flags the freeness hypothesis, which fails over product rings.','Low novelty, high editorial priority: resolve the chosen category before any universal theorem is stated.',['SGA6I','Buhler2009','DoldPuppe1961'])
add(11,'Existence of the cochain-map representing object',[T1+':1955-1997 (137/44)',T2+':1-47;530-543 (137/45,56-57)'],'How to calculate F(x), and does Hom^•(K,C) exist? CL-SA09-137-028; SA09-1/8.','For bounded finite-free K, require the finite sums and indicated kernel in B. For general finitely presented components distinguish cotensors from tensors; unbounded K needs corresponding products. Universal finite disk sums need no arbitrary kernels.','The finite dual equations are checked in proof_audit.md §4; Hua2026 p165 supplies a related finite-free representation. This is an ordinary representing object, not RHom.','The source is conditional, and the sentence at44 continues at45; the package boundary is not a mathematical gap.','Moderate value as a concise lemma with sharp target hypotheses and a notation note.',['Hua2026','Isbell1960'])
add(12,'Which relative exactness axioms are actually needed?',[T2+':172-229;686-708 (137/49-50,60-61)'],'Must composites of Σ-monos and Σ-epis again be admissible; is one of the added requirements enough? CL-SA09-137-030; SA09-3/75.','Work with a Quillen exact structure, or explicitly formulate and prove a weaker structure sufficient for the particular reconstruction. Do not infer pushout/pullback or composition closure from Sex1-2.','Bühler2009 Definition2.1 lists the full exact-category axioms. The uncertain marginal redundancy claim cannot be matched to one precise published implication.','The author adds axioms in stages; no consolidated minimal system is written.','High value and feasible: make an axiom dependency table and test the weak target class on scalar extensions.',['Buhler2009'])
add(13,'Additive evaluation, flatness and essential image',[T2+':258-528 (137/51-56)'],'Il faudrait prouver the universal theorem; is flatness needed; what is the essential image; verify the adjunction. CL-SA09-137-031; SA09-4/5/6/68/70.','For P bounded nonnegative finite-free complexes and degreewise exact Σ, evaluation on C^n=D_{n+1} is fully faithful for additive k-linear B; with kernels it is an equivalence. General relative targets need explicit admissible-kernel conditions.','Hua2026 pp164-165 gives this exact restricted ordinary theorem; our proof_audit.md §5 checks it directly. No flatness of B is used in this finite additive statement. The generalized relative statement is excluded from the reported formal verification.','The manuscript cancels an initial equivalence, replaces its proof, and qualifies the hypotheses. Some questions are answered later on the same pages.','High companion value but limited new mathematics: present the restricted proof and isolate the genuinely relative remainder.',['Hua2026','Buhler2009'])
add(14,'Exact functors versus evaluated resolutions',[T2+':278-301;523-528 (137/51,56)'],'F is Σ-exact iff its evaluated cochain complex is a Σ₀-resolution, verified at least for abelian B with all exact sequences. CL-SA09-137-032; SA09-7.','Prove the equivalence for a specified exact target with all needed admissible kernels and resolution closure, or retain the abelian formulation. Sex1-2 alone do not suffice.','Bühler§12 gives the relevant resolution framework. Hua2026 explicitly leaves this part outside its verified theorem. The earlier first137 note R100 gives a weak-axiom counterexample; our audit retains it as a conditional obstruction, not a refutation under stronger exactness.','The source adds an explicit abelian qualification; no later removal is justified here.','High value and tractable: formalize the minimum target exactness assumptions and test the torsion-disk sequence.',['Buhler2009','Hua2026'])
add(15,'Intrinsic P/Q characterization and cancelled kernel argument',[T2+':547-770 (137/58-63)'],'Determine P intrinsically; verify condition b; construct the kernel in the cancelled59 draft; decide the image of P₁. CL-SA09-137-033/034; SA09-9/10/11/12.','Separate all finite-free bounded complexes P from the split-homology category Q, fix the exact structure, then state the universal exactness-testing property. Preserve the cancelled59 route as drafting history.','Bühler Definition2.1 and Hua2026’s explicit P provide comparison definitions, but do not decide the uncertain handwriting. [Z --2--> Z] distinguishes the two object classes.','Internal revisions and uncertain symbols prevent one formal axiom extraction; the kernel proof sheet is wholly cancelled.','High editorial value: a precise two-category diagram and the torsion example can prevent false equivalences throughout the dossier.',['Buhler2009','Hua2026'])
add(16,'Relative injectives, comparison homotopies and Ext',[T2+':764-770 (137/63-64)'],'Disks are injectives, add Ψ⁰ for projectives; resolutions and one homotopy class of lifts exist; Ext agrees with hyperext. CL-SA09-137-035; SA09-13/14.','After supplying an exact category with enough relative injectives/projectives, apply the augmented comparison theorem and identify Ext in an explicit ambient derived category. Q cannot simply inherit all degreewise split extensions without checking closure.','Bühler Theorem12.4 proves uniqueness up to homotopy under its exact-category hypotheses. Disk generator calculations are direct; the full Q/Ext statement is not identified in the searched literature.','The page compresses several relative-homological assertions and leaves the exact structure implicit.','Moderate to high value: one run can settle generator tests and determine whether the intended Q class supports an exact structure.',['Buhler2009'])
add(17,'Derived evaluation from the universal cochain complex',[T2+':772-778 (137/64-65)'],'On doit pouvoir montrer, sauf erreur, that H^i(F(C•)) is the derived evaluation at Ψ⁰; suggest a derived-category construction. CL-SA09-137-036; SA09-15.','Choose an abelian/adapted functor category in which the universal sequence is evaluation-acyclic and prove the resulting derived functor formula.','Bühler§12 provides resolution methodology; the exact Hua theorem is ordinary, not derived. No opened reference proves the manuscript’s fully relative formulation.','The author explicitly marks both expectation and uncertainty; no proof appears in this range.','High value: a precise small abelian target is a realistic first test before attempting general relative derived categories.',['Buhler2009','Hua2026'])
add(18,'Unital multiplicative generators',[T2+':850-972 (137/67-71)'],'Can multiplicative data be encoded on the universal complex; K has no unit for *; add a unit in P₀ or Q. CL-SA09-137-039; SA09-21/22.','Specify the enlarged generator category containing S₀ and the closed degree-zero unit, then verify generator-level naturality in both variables.','Dold–Puppe§2 supplies the transported tensor; Richter2009§§6-7 studies its chain-side monoids. The kernel-free unit variant still requires an explicit representability formulation.','The missing unit is discovered by the author and repaired only schematically.','High value: the unit enlargement is finite and should be made explicit before extending the product.',['DoldPuppe1961','Richter2009'])
add(19,'Existence in the multiplicative factorization square',[T2+':941-966 (137/70-71)'],'The unknown arrow is uniquely determined through a mono, with a written question mark at the factorization. CL-SA09-137-040; SA09-23/24.','Prove the appropriate two-presentation kernel formula for X*Y and preservation by F, or give a counterexample to the proposed extension under the source’s hypotheses.','The conditional kernel proof is checked in proof_audit.md §6. Bühler’s exactness axioms do not alone imply the required tensor-kernel compatibility; no exact published completion was found.','Monicity proves uniqueness rather than existence; the written question marks the actual missing construction.','Highest near-term priority: one focused run can either prove the kernel lemma or isolate a concrete obstruction.',['Buhler2009','Richter2009'])
add(20,'Choice independence, coherence and kernel-free unit',[T2+':966-972 (137/71)'],'Independence of choices and coherence are called immediate; can the unit be given without requiring Z⁰ to exist? CL-SA09-137-040; SA09-82.','Once the factorization exists naturally, compare common refinements and verify associativity/symmetry/unit diagrams; formulate the unit by compatible maps from1 into degree0 satisfying the differential equation.','The universal-property proof strategy is standard; Berger–Fresse supplies a different higher-coherent model, not this particular strict extension.','The source states the checks without expansion and depends on MP-SA09-19.','High value after the factorization lemma: these finite diagrams can be checked within a few hours.',['BergerFresse2004','Buhler2009'])
add(21,'From cup-product homotopies to structured cochains',[T2+':977-994 (137/72)'],'Obtain the cup product with associativity, signed commutativity and unit, all up to homotopy. CL-SA09-137-041; SA09-25/26.','Keep the stated binary homotopies distinct from a coherent E∞ action; compare via an explicit operation-preserving map if one is desired.','Berger–Fresse2004 constructs a Barratt–Eccles action extending normalized cup multiplication. The interval example here confirms that ordinary Alexander–Whitney multiplication is not strictly graded commutative.','The source expressly qualifies its conclusion by homotopy and does not list higher coherences.','Moderate value: a low-degree comparison is feasible, while a complete equivalence of enhancement theories is a separate large task.',['BergerFresse2004'])
add(22,'Recover the polynomial grading and degree-one structure',[T2+':1036-1119 (137/75-77)'],'The uniqueness argument is withdrawn for arithmetic reasons; an Oubli concerns the degree-one structure. CL-SA09-137-044; SA09-32/33/34/87.','Treat grading/multigrading as data compatible with all base algebras and composition; specify P₁ explicitly rather than detecting it only by integer scalar actions.','Roby’s natural-law definition in SGA4 XVII5.5.2.2 and Friedlander–Suslin Definition2.1 give valid concrete frameworks. F_p and F_p[T] separate scalar tests from polynomial laws.','The counterexample is already recognized by the author; the omitted axiom’s exact wording remains uncertain.','High editorial value: this is the first prerequisite of a defensible full polynomial-category theorem.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','FriedlanderSuslin1997'])
add(23,'Strict representability and triadditivity',[T2+':1096-1198 (137/77-80)'],'Assert triadditivity of P_(1,1), representability by tensor and Γ, and strengthen universal properties with extra parameters. CL-SA09-137-045; SA09-35/36/38.','Impose coherent multigrading and parameter-stable representations; prove the Yoneda comparison maps are isomorphisms rather than deducing that from bare representability alone.','SGA4 XVII5.5.2.3 and5.5.2.6 prove the module example; the full arbitrary-category axiom theorem remains distinct from Roby’s representation theorem.','The needed compatibility is partly imposed and partly asserted; no complete axiom list/proof is provided.','Very high value: a single run can write the precise mixed-degree hypotheses and test whether they are independent.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','Hua2026'])
add(24,'Why is Γ⁰(0) the tensor unit?',[T2+':1143-1174;1193-1196 (137/78-80)'],'Il faut examiner why the proposed unit should be Γ⁰(0). CL-SA09-137-045; SA09-37.','Under the later coherent exponential/multigraded comparison isomorphisms, use the degree(1,0) universal property to prove X⊗Γ⁰(0)≅X.','The page supplies the later conditional argument; SGA4 XVII5.5.2.3/6 gives its module model.','This question is answered later in the same text under stronger assumptions; it is not globally open.','Low standalone priority: record the dependency on MP-SA09-23 and include the short proof in the companion.',['SGA4XVII'])
add(25,'Does binary compatibility imply all arities?',[T2+':1191 (137/80)'],'The NB proposes beginning with r=2. SA09-90; CL-SA09-137-045.','With coherent associativity/symmetry, prove by induction that binary exponential representations yield all finite arities, including zero and one; without those coherences the reduction is not automatic.','The module exponential formula is SGA4 XVII5.5.2.6. No opened source isolates the exact weak abstract hypotheses of this NB.','The source only suggests the reduction.','Moderate value and highly tractable after a complete axiom list is fixed.',['SGA4XVII','Roby1963'])
add(26,'Homogeneous substitution, typed associativity and degree zero',[T2+':1211-1274 (137/81-83)'],'Define α, verify associativity, and add the forgotten degree-zero condition in the converse. CL-SA09-137-047/048; SA09-40/41/42.','Use correctly typed natural α_{p,q}, Γ¹ units and the specified α_{q,0} condition; prove the homogeneous representability equivalence before mixing degrees.','Hua2026 pp166-167 treats the homogeneous core and acknowledges the unconstructed total category; proof_audit.md §6 independently checks the categorical formula.','The author omits checks and then explicitly remembers an axiom; one square label is ill-typed as transcribed.','High editorial value and feasible: formalize the small homogeneous core with a transparent list of excluded structures.',['Hua2026','Roby1963'])
add(27,'The full polynomial/tensor-PD equivalence',[T2+':1278-1284 (137/84)'],'On vérifie, and the two notions are in equivalence. CL-SA09-137-049; SA09-44.','Prove an equivalence including mixed-degree composition, products, additions, constants, strict parameter representations, tensor coherence and exponential Γ, or state the exact additional axioms needed.','Roby1963 and Friedlander–Suslin1997 establish important concrete components. Hua2026 pp166-168 explicitly limits its proof to the homogeneous core and does not settle the full statement.','The source compresses the verification into a sentence after several repaired omissions.','Highest conceptual interest, moderate one-run reach: an axiom/composition audit can determine the precise missing theorem.',['Roby1963','FriedlanderSuslin1997','Hua2026'])
add(28,'Canonical PD structures in an abstract tensor-PD category',[T2+':1292-1303 (137/85-86)'],'When and how do Γ-objects acquire divided powers? The module case is called canonical; a graded example bears a question mark. CL-SA09-137-050; SA09-45/46/47/48.','Require a positive-degree ideal, specify ordinary versus Koszul symmetry, and construct compatible evaluation maps Γ^pΓ^qM→Γ^{pq}M. Do not invert α or put ordinary PD on the unit ideal of Z.','Stacks07GL gives all PD axioms; Richter2009 Definition2.1 distinguishes odd-degree behavior. Rank-one iteration gives the nonunit coefficient3 for p=q=2.','The abstract question is explicit; the surviving lines do not settle ideal or graded-symmetry conventions.','High value: the smallest universal example and typed iteration diagrams can sharply delimit admissible abstract axioms.',['StacksPD','Richter2009','Roby1963'])
add(29,'Polynomial-law enrichment on Hom modules',[T2+':1304-1310 (137/86)'],'When can composition and f↦Γ^p(f) be polynomial of degree p, not merely maps of sets? CL-SA09-137-051; SA09-49.','Specify natural laws over all coefficient algebras with compatible composition in both Hom variables; in an arbitrary tensor category provide the representing enrichment rather than identify scalar homogeneity with a law.','Roby/SGA4 XVII5.5.2 give arbitrary-module laws; Friedlander–Suslin Definition2.1 treats finite-dimensional vector spaces over a field. Neither is literally the unspecified arbitrary tensor-category assertion.','The final question deliberately asks for more structure than the object functors already constructed.','High value and feasible in a restricted setting: write the module proof with exact variance, then isolate its categorical prerequisites.',['Roby1963','SGA4XVII','FriedlanderSuslin1997'])
print(json.dumps({'problems':len(P),'ids':[P[0]['id'],P[-1]['id']]}))
